### Step 2 — Auth. Run top to bottom with VS Code "REST Client".
### The refresh cookie is stored automatically between requests.
@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080

### 1. Sign up → 201 + accessToken + Set-Cookie cookify_refresh (HttpOnly)
# @name signup
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "test_chef",
  "email": "test_chef@cookify.dev",
  "phone": "+919000000001",
  "password": "Cookify2026!",
  "confirmPassword": "Cookify2026!",
  "firstName": "Test",
  "lastName": "Chef"
}

### 2. Same username, different case → 409 USERNAME_TAKEN
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "TEST_CHEF", "email": "other@cookify.dev", "password": "Cookify2026!", "confirmPassword": "Cookify2026!" }

### 3. Weak password (8 chars) + mismatch → 400 with field errors
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "weak_user", "email": "weak@cookify.dev", "password": "short123", "confirmPassword": "nope" }

### 4. Login with email (username or phone also work) → 200
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "identifier": "test_chef@cookify.dev", "password": "Cookify2026!" }

### 5. Wrong password → 401 INVALID_CREDENTIALS
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "identifier": "test_chef", "password": "WrongPass123" }

### 6. Current user (uses token from request 4) → 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

### 7. Current user without token → 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users/me

### 8. Refresh (uses cookie) → 200 + new accessToken + rotated cookie
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/refresh

### 9. Logout → 204, cookie cleared
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/logout

### 10. Refresh after logout → 401 INVALID_REFRESH_TOKEN
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/refresh
